--- body ---
## Context

Child of tracking ticket 0236 (session-trace economics audit), phase 5 —
the final study phase. Phase 4 (0244, closed, PR #378) settled every
screening bound by counterfactual accounting
(docs/trace-counterfactuals-2026-06.md) and routed exactly two measures
to live A/B, because in both cases the cost is entangled with delivery
quality and existing traces never observe the counterfactual:

- **Measure A — model right-sizing of long Opus mains.** Mains are 75%
  of spend; Opus mains sit +1.04 off the pooled cost-vs-turns curve.
  Open question: does a Sonnet main deliver gaze-APPROVED PRs at Opus
  rates?
- **Measure B — verification convergence (single-pass gaze/verify).**
  $259/wk incremental upper bound (vg bucket: turns after the 2nd
  verify/gaze invocation, 44 sessions). Re-entry is NOT explained by
  diff size (re-entry median 465 lines vs 597 single-pass), but the
  bucket contains legitimate round-2 fix work (REROLL loops). Open
  question: how much of the vg bucket is process overhead vs real fixes?

Quality guardrails fixed by phase 4: merged-rate is saturated (112/112),
so the operative metrics are REROLL mentions/PR (baseline 33/112),
ESCALATE mentions (baseline 18), and gaze verdict outcomes.

Honest constraint (study design in 0236): LLM sessions do not replay
deterministically and replays burn real tokens — this phase is narrow by
design. No new census machinery; measurement reuses the committed
scripts. All $ remain shadow dollars (list-price API-equivalents under
subscription auth), stated as such in the report header.

## Relevant files

- `docs/trace-counterfactuals-2026-06.md` — routing decision + guardrail
  baselines (the spec for this phase)
- `scripts/trace-stats.py` — census per-agent cost rows (arm cost
  measurement)
- `scripts/trace-hypotheses.py` — vg-bucket / H13 statistics for
  measure B
- `scripts/trace-pr-join.py` + `docs/trace-pr-join-2026-06.csv` —
  REROLL/ESCALATE guardrail extraction; the join cache accumulates
  across runs
- `skills/beat/SKILL.md`, `skills/gaze/SKILL.md` — intervention surfaces

## Actions

1. **Pin one intervention per measure** (first commit, before any B-arm
   data exists). Defaults, to be confirmed or revised with reasons:
   - A: paired replay — re-run ~5 closed tickets from their original
     base SHA with a Sonnet main (same skill path), compare against the
     original Opus traces: total $, and does the fresh PR pass gaze.
     Paired same-ticket comparison beats week-vs-week for a model
     change that would otherwise put a whole nightbeat week at risk.
   - B: nightbeat-week flag — one week with a convergence rule (e.g.
     after the first full gaze round, REROLL fixes re-check through
     verify-gate only, no full panel re-run). Convergence only fires on
     re-entry events, so a live week is the natural unit.
2. **Pre-register** in `docs/trace-ab-2026-06.md` before B-arm data:
   metric definitions ($ per merged PR / per cycle, REROLL/PR, ESCALATE
   count, gaze verdict distribution), window dates, exclusion rules
   (study-session reflexivity), and the decision rule with thresholds
   (adopt iff cost drops and guardrails hold within stated noise).
3. **A arm**: the existing corpus baseline, already measured — weekly $
   and guardrails from the current census + join cache. No re-runs.
4. **Run the B arms** on the pinned configs. If both run as live weeks,
   run them in disjoint weeks to avoid interaction (pre-register the
   choice).
5. **Harvest**: re-run census + pr-join over the B windows; compute the
   pre-registered metrics; write the verdict per measure.
6. Update tracker 0236: phase 5 done; list what remains for integration
   review (trace-doctor skill assembly; phase-4 adopt items #1
   micro-turn rule and #3 compact-audit advisory if still unowned).

## Test

- Red first for any new script logic: per-window date filtering of
  guardrail metrics gets a fixture (trace rows in/out of window);
  the pre-registered decision rule, implemented as a pure function,
  gets unit tests mapping fixture metric values to expected
  adopt/reject verdicts.

## Verification

- [ ] Interventions and decision rules pre-registered in the report
      BEFORE B-arm data collection (git history proves the ordering)
- [ ] B arms ran on the pinned configs (flag/config visible in history)
- [ ] Metrics computed by committed scripts, reproducible from cached
      inputs without network
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Invariants

- Zero LLM calls in committed scripts; no trace content in committed
  artifacts (PR numbers and aggregates ok)
- Existing census accounting untouched (additive only)
- Verdicts come only from pre-registered metrics — no post-hoc metric
  shopping
- The quality guardrail is binding: a cost win with degraded guardrails
  is a REJECT

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Both measures have a verdict in `docs/trace-ab-2026-06.md`:
      adopt (config-change PR linked) or reject with measured evidence
- [ ] Guardrail metrics reported against the phase-4 baselines
      (REROLL/PR 33/112, ESCALATE 18)
- [ ] Tracker 0236 updated; remaining integration work explicitly
      listed
- [ ] `make check` passes
